{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":68076493,"ns":0,"title":"Frontiers in Public Health","revisions":[{"revid":1370115005,"parentid":1370114537,"minor":false,"timestamp":"2026-08-19T05:31:46Z","size":5598,"sha1":"fc207c15f4c5d991e7c00a99bbd30ecc0aed6c8c","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"{{Infobox journal\n| title = Frontiers in Public Health\n| editor = [[Paolo Vineis]]\n| discipline =\n| abbreviation = Front. Public Health \n| publisher = [[Frontiers Media]]\n| country = \n| frequency = \n| history = 2013–present\n| openaccess =\n| impact = \n| impact-year = \n| website = \n| link1 = \n| link1-name =\n| link1-at = \n| link2 =\n| link2-name =\n| ISSN = 2296-2565\n| eISSN = 2296-2565\n| OCLC = \n}}\n'''''Frontiers in Public Health''''' is a multidisciplinary open-access journal that is published online by [[Frontiers Media]]. The journal covers “occupational, mental and reproductive health, medicine and social policy, epidemiology, rehabilitation, obesity, family and social issues, quality of life and public health education and promotion.”<ref>{{Cite web|title=Frontiers in Public Health {{!}} Journal Report|url=https://reports.frontiersin.org/reports/frontiers-in-public-health-report.html|access-date=2021-08-03|website=reports.frontiersin.org|archive-date=2021-07-24|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210724095417/https://reports.frontiersin.org/reports/frontiers-in-public-health-report.html|url-status=live}}</ref> It is based in Switzerland.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Frontiers in Public Health|url=https://www.scimagojr.com/journalsearch.php?q=21100798718&tip=sid&clean=0|access-date=2021-08-03|website=www.scimagojr.com}}</ref>\n\n== Controversy ==\n{{main|1=Frontiers Media#Controversies}}\nIn late September 2014, ''Frontiers in Public Health'' published a controversial article that supported [[HIV denialism]]; three days later the publisher issued a statement of concern and announced an investigation into the review process of the article.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://retractionwatch.com/2014/09/26/publisher-issues-statement-of-concern-about-hiv-denial-paper-launches-investigation/ |title=Publisher issues statement of concern about HIV denial paper, launches investigation |work=[[Retraction Watch]] |access-date=2015-10-21 |date=2014-09-26 |archive-date=2014-09-29 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140929090928/http://retractionwatch.com/2014/09/26/publisher-issues-statement-of-concern-about-hiv-denial-paper-launches-investigation/ |url-status=live }}</ref> It was eventually decided that the article would not be retracted but instead was reclassified as an opinion piece.<ref name=RWstand>{{cite web|last=Ferguson|first=Cat|title=Frontiers lets HIV denial article stand, reclassifies it as \"opinion\"|url=https://retractionwatch.com/2015/02/24/frontiers-lets-hiv-denier-article-stand-reclassifies-it-as-opinion/|website=Retraction Watch|date=24 February 2015|access-date=15 February 2024|archive-date=16 March 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180316023247/https://retractionwatch.com/2015/02/24/frontiers-lets-hiv-denier-article-stand-reclassifies-it-as-opinion/|url-status=live}}</ref> It has since been retracted.<ref>{{cite journal |title=Questioning the HIV-AIDS hypothesis: 30 years of dissent|year=2014|doi=10.3389/fpubh.2014.00154|pmid=25695040|last1=Goodson|first1=P.|journal=Frontiers in Public Health|volume=2|page=154|pmc=4172096|doi-access=free}}{{Retracted|doi=10.3389/fpubh.2019.00334|pmid=31720286|http://retractionwatch.com/2019/10/25/misguided-and-ineffectual-publisher-offers-mea-culpa-in-retraction-of-paper-questioning-link-between-hiv-and-aids/ ''Retraction Watch''|intentional=yes|doi-access=free}}</ref>\n\nIn June 2016, ''Frontiers in Public Health'' published a [[chemtrail conspiracy theory]] paper.<ref>{{cite web |title=More Fringe Science from Borderline Publisher Frontiers |url=https://scholarlyo.com/more-fringe-science-from-borderline-publisher-frontiers/ |access-date=19 August 2026 |archive-date=19 August 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260819052053/https://scholarlyo.com/more-fringe-science-from-borderline-publisher-frontiers/ |url-status=live }}</ref> It was later retracted.<ref>{{cite web |title=Retraction Human and Environmental Dangers Posed by Ongoing Global Tropospheric Aerosolized Particulates for Weather Modification |url=https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/public-health/articles/10.3389/fpubh.2016.00156/full |access-date=19 August 2026 |archive-date=10 February 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260210122844/https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/public-health/articles/10.3389/fpubh.2016.00156/full |url-status=live }}</ref>\n\nIn November 2016, a paper in ''Frontiers in Public Health'' linking [[autism and vaccines|vaccines to autism]] was provisionally-accepted, then retracted. Public criticism noted the paper relied on flawed methodology for reliable results, basing its conclusions only on an online questionnaire, filled in by 415 mothers of school children who self-reported whether their children had neurodevelopmental disorders, and their vaccination status.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Chawla |first1=Dalmeet Singh |url=https://retractionwatch.com/2016/11/28/study-linking-vaccines-autism-pulled-frontiers-following-heavy-criticism/ |title=Study linking vaccines to autism pulled following heavy criticism |website=[[Retraction Watch]] |date=2016-11-28 |access-date=2018-03-14 |archive-date=2018-03-16 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180316022947/https://retractionwatch.com/2016/11/28/study-linking-vaccines-autism-pulled-frontiers-following-heavy-criticism/ |url-status=live }}</ref>\n\n==References==\n{{Reflist}}\n\n==External links==\n*[https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/public-health Official website]\n*[https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/journals/2277/ National Institutes of Health archive]\n\n[[Category:Frontiers Media academic journals]]"}}}],"contentmodel":"wikitext","pagelanguage":"en","pagelanguagehtmlcode":"en","pagelanguagedir":"ltr","touched":"2026-11-17T20:06:09Z","lastrevid":1370115005,"length":5598}]}}